                <pb facs="0473" n="388" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg388"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/2020: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Jones</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-17T17:00:00-05:48"><hi rendition="#italic">September 17,
                                1919, 5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            September 20, 2.45 p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>General Lopez G. entered Tegucigalpa today at 4 p.m. with approximately 600 men
                    partly armed, without resistance. Little enthusiasm displayed by populace.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jones</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
